-- title:
--   Separability of j(q^N) over K(j(q))
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $N$ be a prime number. Let `data` be an element of `ModularPolynomialData N`, that is, a polynomial $\Phi =$ `data.Φ` in $\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ which is monic (in $Y$), whose degree equals `dedekindPsi N` $= \sum_{d \mid N,\ d\ \text{squarefree}} N/d$ (for $N$ prime this is $N+1$, by [`ModularCurve.dedekindPsi_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.dedekindPsi_prime)), and which satisfies $\Phi(j(q), j(q^N)) = 0$ in the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, the evaluation being made by substituting the rational $q$-expansion `jq` for $X$ and `jqN N` for $Y$. Assume furthermore `EvalSymm data.Φ`: for all Laurent series $x, y$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ one has $\Phi.\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{aeval}\,x)(y) = \Phi.\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{aeval}\,y)(x)$, i.e. the two evaluations of $\Phi$ at $(x,y)$ and at $(y,x)$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ agree. Assume finally that $N$ is invertible in $K$, in the form $(N : K) \neq 0$. Inside the field $K((q))$ of Laurent series over $K$, write $\bar j(q) =$ `jqModC K` for $q^{-1}$ times the power series obtained from `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type numerator by reducing its integer coefficients into $K$, and $\bar j(q^N) =$ `jqNModC K N` for its image under `qExpand`, the ring endomorphism of $K((q))$ multiplying all exponents by $N$. The conclusion is that $\bar j(q^N)$ is separable over the intermediate field $K(\bar j(q))$ of $K((q))$ generated by $\bar j(q)$, i.e. its minimal polynomial over that subfield is a separable polynomial.
--
--   This is the separability of the function-field extension $K(j(q), j(q^N))/K(j(q))$ attached to the modular curve $X_0(N)$ over a base field in which $N$ is invertible, expressed concretely in terms of $q$-expansions. It is used in the analysis of the places of that extension and of the cusp above $q = 0$, and in the finiteness statements for the Hecke correspondence in characteristic prime to $N$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isSeparable_jqNModC_of_modularPolynomialData.lean

